      "difficulty_level": "H2",
      "difficulty_reason": "The author proves convergence by a well-founded padded-column order and identifies the precise tableau normal forms, then constructs finite-state right-multiplication transducers using a single right-to-left normalization pass and derives all four padded multiplier regularity conditions. The bounded three-step critical-branching diagrams supply the coherent extension. This coordinated rewriting/automata/polygraphic construction is retained as one principal presentation object, rather than counting its standard finiteness, PBW, word-problem and categorical-action consequences separately.",
